Fix blank-screen boot crash + boot hardening audit (Task #913)

Root cause: validateIntegrationsBoot() ran at the top of src/main.tsx
before the try/catch that wraps ReactDOM render. Missing AWS/PostHog
keys caused it to throw, module evaluation aborted, and the HTML splash
was hidden in dev — leaving a blank gray page with no diagnostic.

Changes:
- src/main.tsx: moved validateIntegrationsBoot() inside the render
  try/catch so any throw lands on the existing inline Boot Error UI;
  wrapped each pre-render helper (initSentryBoot, startTrace,
  installFetchTracePropagation, initBrowserOtel) in its own try/catch
  so a single failing observability helper can never blank the screen.
- src/lib/integrations/registry.ts: re-tiered enforceInDev — only
  Supabase still blocks dev boot. Mapbox, AWS, Sentry, PostHog are now
  warn-only; each degrades gracefully at runtime.
- src/components/dev/MissingIntegrationsBanner.tsx (new): dev-only
  fixed footer chip listing integrations with missing required env
  vars, with a link to /admin/diagnostics.
- src/App.tsx: lazy-mounted the banner under CoreProviders (dev only)
  and wrapped bootstrapAppRuntime() in try/catch.
- index.html: removed the `if (!isDev)` guard so the HTML radar splash
  is visible in dev too — stalled boots are now visibly stalled instead
  of looking blank. The 15s/6s watchdogs already in place keep working.
- docs/boot-audit.md (new): full per-helper audit of the boot chain
  with tier classification, current protections, and follow-ups.

Verification:
- App now renders the home page with all env vars present.
- With AWS_REGION + PostHog keys absent (current dev state), home page
  renders normally and the dev banner shows "AWS, PostHog".
- Critical-path Boot Error UI in main.tsx remains the fallback for any
  Supabase-tier failure or React crash during initial render.

Out of scope: implementing missing integrations themselves; per-pillar
functional audits; Vercel deploy config.

